# Building a Personal Tutor with Deepseek and JS – Comprehensive Learning Guide

## Course Overview

This course teaches you how to build an AI-powered personal tutor application using JavaScript and the Deepseek API. You'll learn to integrate modern language models into web applications, manage conversational state, handle API interactions, and create interactive learning interfaces. This path is ideal for **intermediate JavaScript developers** who want to understand AI integration, API consumption, and real-world application architecture without deep-dive machine learning knowledge.

**Why it matters for interview prep:**
- Demonstrates full-stack JavaScript competency
- Shows API integration and async/await mastery
- Proves ability to handle real-world requirements (error handling, rate limiting, caching)
- Relevant for roles at AI-forward companies, startups, and modern product teams
- Bridges frontend and backend thinking

## Core Topics Covered

- **API Integration & HTTP Requests** – Calling Deepseek API, handling responses, error management
- **Asynchronous JavaScript** – Promises, async/await, managing concurrent requests
- **State Management** – Tracking conversation history, user sessions, context windows
- **DOM Manipulation & Event Handling** – Building interactive UI for chat interfaces
- **Data Structures for Conversations** – Arrays, objects, and efficient message queuing
- **Environment & Configuration** – API keys, .env files, secure credential handling
- **UI/UX Patterns** – Real-time message rendering, loading states, accessibility
- **Testing & Debugging** – Console logging, API mocking, error scenarios

## Learning Path Workflow

